model {
  extend basalt.productionOps {
    metadata {
      constraint "Abandoned account connections are those that never produced an account, by the same definition as the connections inventory, and expired more than a day ago. The reviewed retention operation removes one organization's abandoned connections that expired before a cutoff at least a day old, at most 200 per plan, after a backup of their full rows and sign-in attempts and a dry run listing their exact IDs and checksums; apply refuses any changed row, removes each sign-in attempt and access row before its connection, and keeps completed connections and every account. The daily rule applies the same definition, keeps a sign-in attempt another connection still names, and runs only when an explicit server setting turns it on; with the setting off it neither connects nor schedules anything. A completed connection remains excluded by the shared produced-account predicate even if later account lifecycle changes leave no live account row. Retention reports typed handled failures through the shared scheduler while keeping its existing quiet HTTP behavior."
    }
  }
}
